    "lawCode": "Amd §679, County L",
    "lawSection": "County Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3637\n\nSPONSOR: ORTT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the county law, in relation to mandatory continuing\neducation requirements for coroners and coroner's deputies\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo require that coroners and coroner deputies, whether elected or\nappointed, shall complete a state-approved course in medical-legal\ninvestigation.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 states that there will be a training requirement for coroners\nand coroner's deputies, they shall successfully complete the training.\nThe coroner or coroner deputy wilt cover the cost. However, at the\ndiscretion of the county they may be reimbursed for alt or a portion of\nthat training fee.\n\nAlso, the coroner or coroner deputy shall attend and successfully\ncompete no less than 30 credits in a state-approved medical legal inves-\ntigation courses over a 3-year period. Additionally, each coroner and\ncoroner deputy shall be exempt from the training for one year following\ntheir appointment.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, New York State does not require a continued education class\nfor coroners or coroner deputies. This bill would allow them to keep up\nwith the changing science of medical-legal investigation to excel and\ncontinue to do the excellent work that they do in the community.  This\nwas at the request of the New York State Association of County Coroners\nand Medical Examiners (NYSACCME).\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-2024: S.9578 Referred to Local Government\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall have become a law\n",
